error BYN2802: `S.run` is `void run() fails F` but `IRun` requires `void run() fails E`

  10 │     void run() fails {
     │          ^^^ infers `F`, which `IRun.run` does not declare
     │
  help: change the signature to `void run() fails E` and handle the other errors inside `S.run`

warning BYN2311: `a` is never reassigned; declare it with `let`

  16 │     var a = S<i64> { v: 1 }
     │         ^
     │
  help: declare it with `let` to tell the reader the value never changes
     │ 16 │     let a = S<i64> { v: 1 }
     │    │     +++

warning BYN2311: `b` is never reassigned; declare it with `let`

  17 │     var b = S<bool> { v: true }
     │         ^
     │
  help: declare it with `let` to tell the reader the value never changes
